#: src/error-handling/panics.md:6
msgid "Panics"
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:8
msgid "In case of a fatal runtime error, Rust triggers a \"panic\":"
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:11 src/error-handling/panics.md:35
msgid "// Copyright 2022 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:12 src/error-handling/panics.md:36
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:20
msgid "Panics are for unrecoverable and unexpected errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:21
msgid "Panics are symptoms of bugs in the program."
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:22
msgid "Runtime failures like failed bounds checks can panic."
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:23
msgid "Assertions (such as `assert!`) panic on failure."
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:24
msgid "Purpose-specific panics can use the `panic!` macro."
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:25
msgid ""
"A panic will \"unwind\" the stack, dropping values just as if the functions "
"had returned."
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:27
msgid ""
"Use non-panicking APIs (such as `Vec::get`) if crashing is not acceptable."
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:32
msgid ""
"By default, a panic will cause the stack to unwind. The unwinding can be "
"caught:"
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:41
msgid "\"No problem here!\""
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:45
msgid "\"oh no!\""
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:51
msgid ""
"Catching is unusual; do not attempt to implement exceptions with "
"`catch_unwind`!"
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:53
msgid ""
"This can be useful in servers which should keep running even if a single "
"request crashes."
msgstr ""

#: src/error-handling/panics.md:55
msgid "This does not work if `panic = 'abort'` is set in your `Cargo.toml`."
msgstr ""
